/*
  Watcher Mochi animations adapted for ESP32-C3 Super Mini + ST7789P3 SPI TFT.

  Source project used as reference/assets:
    https://github.com/pham-tuan-binh/watcher-mochi

  Original watcher-mochi is an ESP-IDF SenseCAP Watcher project using SD-card
  GIF files, LVGL, touch, sound, and ESP32-S3 board APIs. This file is a
  standalone Arduino IDE port for your hardware: it embeds a curated subset of
  the watcher-mochi GIF animations as 1-bit frames and renders them directly to
  the ST7789 display. No SD card, LVGL, touch, or speaker is required.

  Hardware pin map, fixed for this build:
    BL  -> GPIO 21, ACTIVE LOW: LOW = backlight ON, HIGH = OFF
    CS  -> GPIO 10
    DC  -> GPIO 8
    RST -> GPIO 7
    SDA -> GPIO 6  (SPI MOSI)
    SCL -> GPIO 4  (SPI CLK)
    VCC -> 3.3V
    GND -> GND

  Libraries for Arduino IDE:
    - Adafruit GFX Library
    - Adafruit ST7735 and ST7789 Library

  Notes:
    - Frame data below was generated from watcher-mochi/sd_content/*.gif.
    - GIF animations are property of Dasai and are included by watcher-mochi for
      personal use. Keep this as a personal desk/toy project.
*/

